---

<section id="spaces" class="py-24 sm:py-36 bg-warm-canvas/60 border-y border-charcoal-border-subtle">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10 space-y-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-idle-green">
        02 / Spaces & Profiles
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal leading-[1.05]">
        One browser. <br/>
        <span class="font-serif italic font-normal text-idle-green">Many lives.</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg sm:text-xl text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed font-normal pt-2">
        <p>
          Your work projects shouldn't be tangled up with holiday plans, shopping lists, and that recipe you'll never make.
        </p>
        <p>
          Idle gives everything its own space, without filling your desktop with windows.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Three sub-features -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 pt-4">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal">A space for everything</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed">
          Keep work, personal projects, and late-night rabbit holes in their own spaces. Each with its own tabs and groups.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed pt-1">
          Switch between them instantly. No window juggling required.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal">Separate accounts. Zero awkwardness.</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed">
          Work login? Personal login? Three different accounts for the same website?
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed pt-1">
          Profiles keep your sessions properly separated, so your accounts don't accidentally mingle.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal">Right where you left it</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed">
          Close Idle. Restart your computer. Go make a cup of tea.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed pt-1">
          Your tabs and spaces will be waiting when you get back. Just as you left them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
